<body>
  <h1>connectDevices</h1>
  <p>A Python-based project enabling seamless communication and data exchange between devices using socket programming. This project is designed for real-time communication, file sharing, folder sharing, and command execution between connected devices.</p>
  
  <h2>Features</h2>
  <div class="feature">
    <h3>1. Real-Time Chat</h3>
    <p>Enables real-time messaging between two connected devices with a simple and intuitive interface.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature">
    <h3>2. File Sharing</h3>
    <p>Facilitates fast and reliable file transfer between devices. Adjust the performance by modifying the <code>chunk_size</code> parameter (default: 5000 bytes).</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature">
    <h3>3. Folder Sharing</h3>
    <p>Supports sharing entire folders, including subfolders and their contents, in a single operation. Primarily designed for sharing all photos or any other folder.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature">
    <h3>4. Command Execution</h3>
    <p>Allows one device to send shell commands to another device for execution. The output or error is returned to the original device.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Technologies Used</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Programming Language:</strong> Python</li>
    <li><strong>Libraries:</strong> socket, os, threading, contextlib</li>
    <li><strong>Platforms:</strong> Cross-platform (Windows, Linux, Mobile)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Usage</h2>
  <pre>
  # Clone the repository
  git clone https://github.com/aditya7balotra/connectDevices.git

  # Navigate to the desired branch
  git checkout branch_name

  # Run the server
  python server.py

  # Run the client
  python client.py
  </pre>

  <h2>Branches</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>chat:</strong> Real-time messaging</li>
    <li><strong>shareFiles:</strong> File sharing between devices</li>
    <li><strong>shareAllPhotos:</strong> Folder sharing functionality</li>
    <li><strong>cmd:</strong> Remote command execution</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Project Demonstration</h2>
  <p>Check out the project demo videos on LinkedIn showcasing the various functionalities, including chat, file sharing, and folder sharing.</p>

